# What the source distribution carries beyond the package itself. README and
# LICENSE arrive on their own, named by `readme` and `license-files`. All three
# of the paths named here are symlinks into the repository root, because
# setuptools reads nothing outside this directory; the sdist gets the real
# bytes, since the archive follows the link rather than recording it.
#
# The test suite is deliberately absent. `tools/hmd/tests` would now travel
# cleanly — the repository-wide guards that could not, `test_docs.py` and
# `test_mkdocs.py`, live at the repository root and are not part of this
# project — but gates are run from a checkout, not from an sdist, and shipping
# a suite invites someone to run it as if it were one.
include CHANGELOG.md

# The runnable fixture the README tells a new reader to lint first. 60K, and it
# is the only way `hmd lint --root examples/small` works straight out of the
# archive.
recursive-include examples *.hmd *.md *.toml
